			"color":"#432",
			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action cinematic style, horizontal 16:9, 8.00 seconds total, soft natural daylight filtering through a bamboo canopy, clean full-frame footage. Chest-up close-up, centered composition, shallow depth of field. A voluptuous beautiful young Asian woman dressed as a ninja in a fitted white outfit — white crossed-collar top with a wide white waist sash and subtle silver trim, long black hair partially tied up with a white ribbon, loose strands framing her face — stands among tall green bamboo, the wrapped hilt of her sword visible over her right shoulder. Static shot with a very slow push-in of small amplitude. At 0.00 seconds her eyes are closed, expression serene; she inhales slowly and deeply, chest visibly rising with the breath, shoulders settling downward. At 1.20 seconds she opens her eyes, gaze sharp and focused, lips set with quiet determination. [Shot 2] At 00:02.000, the camera cuts to a full-body wide shot deep in the bamboo grove. There is a clear hard cut to a new action state; the previous breathing pause has completely ended before this shot begins. She bursts into motion: drawing the sword in one smooth arc, stepping and dodging left then right with agile footwork, swinging the blade in wide horizontal and diagonal slashes, white sleeves and ribbons streaming behind her. The camera follows her laterally as a tracking shot with medium amplitude and normal speed. As she moves, wind rises through the grove: bamboo stalks sway and bend, green leaves swirl through the air, her hair and sash whip in the gusts, and each slash leaves a bright glinting arc. She alternates left and right dodges with continuous readable footwork until 5.00 seconds. [Shot 3] At 00:05.000, the camera cuts to a frontal medium shot. She completes a final flourish, spins the sword once around her wrist and smoothly sheathes the blade with a crisp click, hands falling calm to her sides. For one brief beat everything is still. Then, in rapid succession, the surrounding bamboo stalks tilt and crash down to the ground behind her one after another, while she stands perfectly composed at the center. The camera begins a steady push-in at slow speed with medium amplitude, gliding from the medium shot into a tight close-up of her stunningly beautiful face: flawless skin, calm confident eyes, a faint serene smile, loose strands of hair and a few drifting leaves passing the frame. The push-in settles at 8.00 seconds with her face filling the frame in soft light.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA bamboo grove ambience starting with a soft breeze, then a rising wind through leaves; sharp sword whooshes and a bright metallic ring of the blade during the performance; quick soft footfalls on leaf-littered ground and cloth rustle; one crisp click as the sword is sheathed; then a cascade of cracking, crashing bamboo falling behind her; finally only a gentle settling wind and faint leaf rustle.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nA low cinematic score at about 80 BPM with deep taiko pulses, sparse plucked strings and one sustained erhu note, dynamics rising through the sword sequence; the score cuts to silence at the moment the sword is sheathed, leaving only the bamboo crash and wind for the final push-in.",
				1344,
				768,
				73
			],
